# implements-port slice 4 under --walk-methods: unit_s4_ret_conv_range.lm2's exact shape, re-staged
# under its own Name so this row runs WITH the knob.  A return's edge makes `go` throwing (its
# implicit `convert`), and a throwing method is outside the walkable subset (l2_rw_may) -- it stays
# native under the knob, as with a store's or an argument's edge, and the root receives the same
# status 3.
fn: go () int
    size_t: b 3000000000U
    return: b
end: go
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: go(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
